2 - 114}{3}\n\\]\n\nWith \\( S^2 = 93 \\):\n\n\\[\nP = \\frac{2 \\times 93 - 114}{3} = 24\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( xy + yz + xz \\) is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).", "ground_truth_solution": "\nGiven the system of equations for positive numbers \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx^2 + xy + y^2 = 48 \\\\\ny^2 + yz + z^2 = 9 \\\\\nz^2 + xz + x^2 = 57\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the expression \\(xy + yz + xz\\).\n\n#### Step 1: Triangle Representation\nConsider points \\(O\\), \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\) such that:\n- \\(\\angle AOB = 120^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle BOC = 120^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle COA = 120^\\circ\\)\n\nPlace \\(x = OA\\), \\(y = OB\\), and \\(z = OC\\).\n\n#### Step 2: Cosine Law Application\nUsing the cosine law in a triangle where the angle between each side is \\(120^\\circ\\), we have:\n- For triangle \\(OAB\\):\n\\[\nAB^2 = OA^2 + OB^2 + OA \\cdot OB \\cdot (-1/2) \\implies x^2 + y^2 + xy \\cdots (1)\n\\]\nGiven:\n\\[\nAB^2 = 48 \\implies x^2 + xy + y^2 = 48\n\\]\n\n- For triangle \\(BOC\\):\n\\[\nBC^2 = OB^2 + OC^2 + OB \\cdot OC \\cdot (-1/2) \\implies y^2 + z^2 + yz \\cdots (2)\n\\]\nGiven:\n\\[\nBC^2 = 9 \\implies y^2 + yz + z^2 = 9\n\\]\n\n- For triangle \\(COA\\):\n\\[\nCA^2 = OC^2 + OA^2 + OC \\cdot OA \\cdot (-1/2) \\implies z^2 + x^2 + xz \\cdots (3)\n\\]\nGiven:\n\\[\nCA^2 = 57 \\implies z^2 + xz + x^2 = 57\n\\]\n\n#### Step 3: Summing the Equations\nAdding all three equations:\n\\[\n(x^2 + xy + y^2) + (y^2 + yz + z^2) + (z^2 + xz + x^2) = 48 + 9 + 57\n\\]\n\\[\n2(x^2 + y^2 + z^2) + (xy + yz + xz) = 114\n\\]\n\n#### Step 4: Solve for \\(xy + yz + xz\\)\nWe know:\n\\[\n2(x^2 + y^2 + z^2) + (xy + yz + xz) = 114\n\\]\n\nLet:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 + z^2 + (xy + yz + xz) = A\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 + z^2 = A - (xy + yz + xz)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting back:\n\\[\n2(A - (xy + yz + xz)) + (xy + yz + xz) = 114\n\\]\n\nLet:\n\\[\nA = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + xy + yz + xz\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n2A - (xy + yz + xz) = 114\n\\]